Shell Scripting:

1. shell : it is an interface between user and OS

2. Types of shell:
--> sh (Bourn shell)
--> ksh (korn shell)
--> csh (C shell)
--> zsh (z shell)
--> fish 
--> bash 

to check out current shell: $SHELL or $0 
check all system supported shell: /etc/shells file

Shell scritpting:
--> Shell scripting is the process of writing a set of linux commands in afile so that they can execute automatically.

what is shebang line?
--> #!/bin/bash
----> it is used to instruct OS to use bash as a command interpreter
----> shebang refers to # and !. in musical notation # called sharp and ! called bang
----> shebang line specifing the interpreter.

**How to run a script:
1. make sure script has execute permission
2. run using:
i] syntax1 =   ./<script_name>
eg: ./1.sh
--> if you are in same directory as the script use relative path

ii] syntax2 =  /path/<script_name>
eg: /etc/1.sh
--> if you are in different directory use absolute path

iii] syntax3 = bash <script_name>
eg: bash 1.sh
--> you are explicitly tell the shell to execute the script using a specific interpreter,  even if it 
does not have execute permission or a shebang line.



